{"id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:line-exists-metric","title":"lem:line-exists-metric","path":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature.md","line":103,"body":"","kind":"lemma","status":"not_started","tex":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature.tex#lem:line-exists-metric","uses":["[[references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#def:minimizing-geodesic-window]]","[[references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#def:has-min-segments]]","[[references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#def:space-of-ends]]","[[references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:ultrafilter-limit-minimizing]]","[[references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:ends-differ-at-compact]]","[[references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:end-component-unbounded]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature.tex","label":"lem:line-exists-metric","line":201,"source":"\\begin{lemma}[Lines from two ends: metric version]\n\\label{lem:line-exists-metric}\n\n\\source{morgan-tian}\n\\uses{def:minimizing-geodesic-window, def:has-min-segments, def:space-of-ends}\n\n\n\n\n\nA proper metric space with minimizing segments and at least two ends\ncontains a minimizing line.\n\\end{lemma}\n\\begin{proof}\n\\sketch\n\n\\uses{lem:ultrafilter-limit-minimizing,lem:ends-differ-at-compact,lem:end-component-unbounded}\nChoose a compact $K$ separating components $U_1,U_2$ selected by two\nends. Pick $x_k\\in U_1$ and $y_k\\in U_2$ at distance at least $k$ from\n$K$. Every minimizing segment from $x_k$ to $y_k$ meets $K$; recenter at\nsuch an intersection. Both parameter endpoints then tend to infinity,\nwhile the new origins remain in $K$. The ultrafilter limit lemma with\n$I=\\Ar$ gives a minimizing line.\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Lemma</div></section>[Lines from two ends: metric version] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6c656d3a6c696e652d6578697374732d6d6574726963\"></span> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source\" style=\"display:block\">Source: <span class=\"reference\">morgan-tian</span></span> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FMorganTian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature%23def%3Aminimizing-geodesic-window\">↗ def:minimizing-geodesic-window</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FMorganTian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature%23def%3Ahas-min-segments\">↗ def:has-min-segments</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FMorganTian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature%23def%3Aspace-of-ends\">↗ def:space-of-ends</a> <p></p>A proper metric space with minimizing segments and at least two ends contains a minimizing line.  <section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p>\\sketch </p><p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FMorganTian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature%23lem%3Aultrafilter-limit-minimizing\">↗ lem:ultrafilter-limit-minimizing</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FMorganTian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature%23lem%3Aends-differ-at-compact\">↗ lem:ends-differ-at-compact</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FMorganTian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature%23lem%3Aend-component-unbounded\">↗ lem:end-component-unbounded</a> Choose a compact <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$K$\">$K$</span> separating components <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$U_1,U_2$\">$U_1,U_2$</span> selected by two ends. Pick <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$x_k\\in U_1$\">$x_k\\in U_1$</span> and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$y_k\\in U_2$\">$y_k\\in U_2$</span> at distance at least <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$k$\">$k$</span> from <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$K$\">$K$</span>. Every minimizing segment from <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$x_k$\">$x_k$</span> to <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$y_k$\">$y_k$</span> meets <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$K$\">$K$</span>; recenter at such an intersection. Both parameter endpoints then tend to infinity, while the new origins remain in <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$K$\">$K$</span>. The ultrafilter limit lemma with <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$I=\\Ar $\">$I=\\Ar $</span> gives a minimizing line. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: sketch"]},"previous":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:end-component-unbounded","next":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:geodesic-continuous-dependence","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#def:minimizing-geodesic-window","title":"def:minimizing-geodesic-window","label":"def:minimizing-geodesic-window"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#def:has-min-segments","title":"def:has-min-segments","label":"def:has-min-segments"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#def:space-of-ends","title":"def:space-of-ends","label":"def:space-of-ends"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:ultrafilter-limit-minimizing","title":"lem:ultrafilter-limit-minimizing","label":"lem:ultrafilter-limit-minimizing"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:ends-differ-at-compact","title":"lem:ends-differ-at-compact","label":"lem:ends-differ-at-compact"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:end-component-unbounded","title":"lem:end-component-unbounded","label":"lem:end-component-unbounded"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#ends","title":"ends","label":"ends"}],"copy_context":{"version":1,"level":0,"node":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:line-exists-metric","title":"lem:line-exists-metric","tex":"\\begin{lemma}[Lines from two ends: metric version]\n\\label{lem:line-exists-metric}\n\n\\source{morgan-tian}\n\\uses{def:minimizing-geodesic-window, def:has-min-segments, def:space-of-ends}\n\n\n\n\n\nA proper metric space with minimizing segments and at least two ends\ncontains a minimizing line.\n\\end{lemma}\n\\begin{proof}\n\\sketch\n\n\\uses{lem:ultrafilter-limit-minimizing,lem:ends-differ-at-compact,lem:end-component-unbounded}\nChoose a compact $K$ separating components $U_1,U_2$ selected by two\nends. Pick $x_k\\in U_1$ and $y_k\\in U_2$ at distance at least $k$ from\n$K$. Every minimizing segment from $x_k$ to $y_k$ meets $K$; recenter at\nsuch an intersection. Both parameter endpoints then tend to infinity,\nwhile the new origins remain in $K$. The ultrafilter limit lemma with\n$I=\\Ar$ gives a minimizing line.\n\\end{proof}","source":"tex/references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature.tex","desc